      "problem": "The Ephesians dossier supplies only the historical Catholic Encyclopedia captivity alternatives and a generic destination qualification, then explicitly declines a current comparison after recorded access failures. It never supplies the principal modern critical authorship/composition horizon required by the 1962 dossier rules, which must already have a reviewed home here before the concise opening is written. The official USCCB Ephesians introduction is now directly readable at https://bible.usccb.org/bible/ephesians/0: its concluding paragraphs distinguish the traditional captivity account from the secretary/later-disciple alternatives and explain the textual and stylistic grounds for uncertainty. Merely saying that the displayed dates are not modern consensus leaves that required historical account absent.",
